# M39 (PLAN_BROWSER_PERF_SECURITY.md §2.10, D49) — isolated POST-uncontended rung against the real
# dogfood target: `POST /cart/items`, a static (non-interpolated, no capture) body against a
# per-user cart row (no shared row lock across VUs — unlike the acceptance scenario's checkout,
# every VU only ever touches its own cart), matching M34's own "POST /cart/items only, static body,
# uncontended" row. `productId` below is the real "Load Test Widget" product's id, resolved once by
# hand before writing this fixture (`GET /products?q=Load%20Test%20Widget`) — hardcoded rather than
# captured so the load run itself pays for zero capture/interpolation overhead, isolating the raw
# POST-with-body cost the same way M34's original row did. Re-resolve and update this id if the
# stack's DB is ever reseeded (a fresh `node cli.mjs start` after `stop` gets a new random UUID —
# perf-0's product row has no pinned id, see testFlow-tests apiV2/src/seed/seed.ts). Same ramp shape
# as checkout-burst.tflw for apples-to-apples comparison against the contended rung.

test "M39 dogfood POST-uncontended" as load
  ramp to 60 users over 20s
  api POST /cart/items body { productId: "6c0b2198-a3c4-4fe0-8aae-64a6714fff3c", quantity: 1 }
  expect status equals 201
